# tripbox settings. Copy to .env beside compose.yaml (chmod 600) and set TRIPBOX_PASSWORD.
# Every other line is optional: a feature is on when its settings are set.
# "docker compose run --rm worker tripbox doctor" says what is missing or wrong.
# A commented line shows the default, or an example where one helps. A value is written as it
# is: no quotes and no space before a #; a literal $ is written $$.

# --- The page ---
# The page's password, 10 characters or more (secret).
TRIPBOX_PASSWORD=
# Who may open the page: password, proxy (a login proxy), cloudflare (Access) or none.
# TRIPBOX_AUTH=password
# Instead of the password, never with it: the whole line tripbox passwd prints.
# TRIPBOX_PASSWORD_HASH=
# With cloudflare: the Zero Trust team name, the part before .cloudflareaccess.com.
# TRIPBOX_ACCESS_TEAM=example-team
# With cloudflare: the audience tag of the Access application that protects the page.
# TRIPBOX_ACCESS_AUD=
# With cloudflare: comma-separated addresses that may open the page.
# TRIPBOX_ALLOWED_EMAILS=alex@example.com
# With proxy: the addresses or networks the login proxy connects from.
# TRIPBOX_TRUSTED_PROXIES=192.0.2.10
# With proxy: the header the proxy names the signed-in user in.
# TRIPBOX_PROXY_USER_HEADER=Remote-User
# With proxy: the user names the proxy may sign in, comma-separated.
# TRIPBOX_PROXY_USERS=alex
# The address people open the page at, a path allowed: every link is built from it.
# TRIPBOX_BASE_URL=https://trips.example.com
# Where the page listens: 127.0.0.1:8110 for this computer only, 0.0.0.0:8110 for every network.
# TRIPBOX_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8110
# The address of the page's source code, which its about line links.
# TRIPBOX_SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/Good-Work-Dojo/tripbox
# Saved copies of the list and each trip opened, for use offline: true or false.
# TRIPBOX_OFFLINE=

# --- Core ---
# The time zone tripbox works in, an IANA name.
# TZ=America/Chicago
# Comma-separated codes of airports you live near: a trip is titled by another one.
# TRIPBOX_HOME_AIRPORTS=MSP

# --- Mail ---
# The IMAP server's name alone.
# TRIPBOX_MAIL_HOST=imap.gmail.com
# The mailbox's login; an email address is shown on the page as the one to forward to.
# TRIPBOX_MAIL_USER=trips@example.com
# The mailbox's password or app password (secret); spaces are removed.
# TRIPBOX_MAIL_PASSWORD=
# Comma-separated addresses whose mail is read; any other mail is rejected unparsed.
# TRIPBOX_MAIL_ALLOWED_SENDERS=alex@example.com
# gmail: a forward is believed only if Google vouches for it; mailbox: other servers.
# TRIPBOX_MAIL_TRUST=gmail
# Domains whose forwarded flights reach AirTrail unseen; unset, the shipped list.
# TRIPBOX_MAIL_TRUSTED_SENDER_DOMAINS=
# labels: handled mail is copied into tripbox/ folders; none: the mailbox is left.
# TRIPBOX_MAIL_FILING=

# --- The model ---
# Who reads emails with no structured data: anthropic, openai (any such server), none.
# TRIPBOX_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# The model's key (secret); a server of your own may need none.
# TRIPBOX_LLM_API_KEY=
# The model's name; with openai, one your server serves.
# TRIPBOX_LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# With openai, your server's address as the worker reaches it, not localhost (secret).
# TRIPBOX_LLM_BASE_URL=http://models.example:11434/v1
# The most a priced model may cost in a month (UTC), in US dollars; 0: never asked.
# TRIPBOX_LLM_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=5.00
# How many calls a day (UTC) a model with no known price may be asked.
# TRIPBOX_LLM_MAX_CALLS_PER_DAY=100
# INPUT,OUTPUT in US dollars per million tokens, for a model tripbox has no price for.
# TRIPBOX_LLM_PRICE_USD_PER_MTOK=

# --- AirTrail ---
# The address AirTrail answers at, as the worker reaches it.
# TRIPBOX_AIRTRAIL_URL=http://flightlog.example:3000
# An API key made in AirTrail under its security settings (secret).
# TRIPBOX_AIRTRAIL_API_KEY=
# true: nothing is written to AirTrail and flights wait; false sends them.
# TRIPBOX_AIRTRAIL_DRY_RUN=true
# The address you open AirTrail at in a browser: the trips list links it.
# TRIPBOX_AIRTRAIL_PUBLIC_URL=https://flightlog.example

# --- Enrichment ---
# Fills in landed flights in AirTrail: aeroapi, or empty for none.
# TRIPBOX_ENRICH=aeroapi
# The flight-data service key (secret): it fills in AirTrail's flights once landed.
# TRIPBOX_AEROAPI_KEY=
# The most to spend on lookups in a calendar month, in US dollars.
# TRIPBOX_AEROAPI_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=1.00
# The most lookups in one run.
# TRIPBOX_AEROAPI_MAX_CALLS_PER_RUN=10

# --- Notifications ---
# Your Telegram bot's token (secret).
# TRIPBOX_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# The Telegram chat that gets the messages and may command the bot.
# TRIPBOX_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# With or instead of Telegram: your ntfy topic's whole address (secret).
# TRIPBOX_NTFY_URL=https://ntfy.example/trips
# An access token for the topic, for a server that asks for one (secret).
# TRIPBOX_NTFY_TOKEN=

# --- Docker Compose ---
# The image the services run.
# TRIPBOX_IMAGE=ghcr.io/good-work-dojo/tripbox:1
# The user id the services run as: the owner of the install's folders.
# TRIPBOX_UID=1000
# The group id the services run as.
# TRIPBOX_GID=1000
# Runs the Telegram bot as well, with the Telegram settings above.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=telegram
